  "description": "The existing timber windows are dated, in poor condition, and no longer meet the needs of the residents. They are causing heat loss, condensation, and other condition-related defects. It is therefore proposed that all windows to the property be replaced with upgraded modern double-glazed uPVC units, which will significantly improve the property’s thermal performance.\n\nThe replacement windows will be designed to reflect the appearance of the originals, with upper and lower opening casements to create a more vertically symmetrical look. They will be finished in an anthracite grey foil wrap (RAL 7016). \n\nThe front entrance doors will be retained, while the rear exit and balcony doors will be replaced to match the new windows.",
